{{wikipedia|Prosthesis}}
==English==

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|la}} from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|πρόσθεσις||addition|sc=Polytonic|tr=prosthesis|lang=grc}}, from {{term|προστίθημι||I add|sc=Polytonic|tr=prostithēmi|lang=grc}}, from {{term|πρός||towards|sc=Polytonic|tr=pros|lang=grc}} + {{term|τίθημι||I place|sc=Polytonic|tr=tithēmi|lang=grc}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|prostheses}}

# An artificial [[replacement]] for a body part, either internal or external.
# {{linguistics}} [[prothesis]]

